{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.15","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[{"sourceType":"datasetVersion","sourceId":2542390}],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"f489b943-f8df-4b94-9dca-482706c2a584","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# Brain Tumor Segmentation - U-Net++ + Adadelta (PyTorch, BraTS 2021) - Kaggle edition\n\n**250 patients x 3 seeds** (seeds 42, 43, 44).\n\n- A fixed pool of 250 patients is cached once. For **each seed** the pool is re-split patient-wise into **60 % train / 20 % val / 20 % test** (150/50/50), and model init + augmentation + batch order also follow that seed.\n- The same seeds give the **same splits in every model notebook** (Basic U-Net, Attention U-Net, DeepLabV3+), so models are compared on identical data per seed.\n- Final table: **mean +/- std over the 3 seeds** (`summary_*.csv`), plus one row per seed in `experiments.csv/xlsx`.\n- Anti-overfitting settings: `BASE_FILTERS = 32`, `WEIGHT_DECAY = 1e-3`, more patients, augmentation, early stopping.\n\n### Before you run\n1. **Add data:** right side panel -> *Add Input* -> search **BraTS 2021** (task 1 training data) -> *Add*.\n   Extracted `*_flair.nii.gz` folders and `.tar` archives are both handled (only the first 250 patients are unpacked from a tar).\n2. **Accelerator:** *Settings -> Accelerator -> GPU* (T4 / P100).\n3. **Internet** is optional (only for `pip install thop` / `torchinfo`).\n4. Three full trainings run back-to-back. `TIME_BUDGET_HOURS` (config cell) stops training in time so finished seeds are never lost; seeds that do not fit are skipped.\n\nSlice cache -> `/kaggle/temp` (not saved with